{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"qaoa-finite-size","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:3206447b7c5ce37e42a253ccbbdf9ea9fd64af6c402a7a116e30915fbcfcd2a4/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618","passage_ref":"sha256:fa472c25832b36a2061f212196277009f716c230a658520bb4b4f2ed8173d74b/papers/long.md/sha256:3206447b7c5ce37e42a253ccbbdf9ea9fd64af6c402a7a116e30915fbcfcd2a4/papers/long.json/passages/qaoa-finite-size","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=long&passage=qaoa-finite-size","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=long&passage=qaoa-finite-size","span":{"end_byte":239543,"end_line":5275,"start_byte":236442,"start_line":5203},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&view=arguments&node=circuit.later_finite_size_comparison&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&node=circuit.later_finite_size_comparison&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&node=circuit.later_finite_size_comparison&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&view=arguments&node=circuit.later_finite_size_comparison&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&ref=sha256%3A47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.later_finite_size_comparison","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The displayed finite estimate is quoted from the later arXiv:2609.40309v1 Corollary S3.1; the growing-depth consequence is the authored elementary deduction log log T_p=4p log p+O(p+log p) with epsilon_p=exp(-p^2). For SK, c_2=1/sqrt(2) matches the unordered-pair expectation after an independent mean-zero scalar diagonal offset. This does not show that the earlier near-optimal constructed words share a uniform angle bound, supply angle-selection complexity, or establish a growing-depth measurement tail. It is standalone context, not a prerequisite of the earlier SK QAOA construction or a selected formal endpoint.","citation_ids":["qaoa_finite_size_corollary","authored_bounded_angle_depth_comparison"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024"],"id":"circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","kind":"claim","label":"A later finite-size estimate for a bounded-angle class","locator":"Corollary S3.1, printed pp.46–47, equations (S3.1)–(S3.4), with cost-angle convention (S3.7). Statement inspected; full cavity proof not independently checked. Authored consequence: long §11.5.","source_id":"qaoa_finite_size_2026","statement":"For the source ordered-tuple Gaussian finite-degree mixture xi(t)=sum_q c_q^2 t^q, a depth p>=1 word with every cost angle bounded in absolute value by Gamma>0, and x>0 with xi(2),xi′(1),xi′′(33)<=x and Gamma^2 p^2 x>=1, set B_p=256p^4(2e Gamma^2 p^2 x)^p, E_p=70 Gamma^2 p^2 x+p log(2), R_p=(2E_p/log(2))^(2p). For 0<epsilon<=4 Gamma p x min(exp(-1/2),2^(-(8p^2+3)/100)), the disorder-averaged energy error |nu_n-nu_infinity| is at most epsilon whenever n>=T_p=max{2^(8p^2+3) B_p (2^(deg(xi)+4) Gamma^2 p^2 x^2/epsilon^2)^R_p [2 log_2(4 Gamma p x/epsilon)+deg(xi)]^2,16 Gamma p x/epsilon}. No mixer-angle bound is imposed. Consequently, for fixed mixture,Gamma,x, deterministic words with p(n)→infinity, one common cost-angle bound Gamma, and p(n)log p(n)=o(log log n) satisfy |nu_n(W_n)-nu_infinity(W_n)|<=exp(-p(n)^2) eventually.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","id":"field:ac9fbb38ea9a547b8673cbb81c35024219ecd9e63f717e067998b997a2a0a491","kind":"evidence_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"evidence_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/evidence/ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","id":"field:c7c8e6549c04f07322f4134917273d6c8c286678dcdab49f732661fae70b4875","kind":"source_id","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"source_id","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/sources/qaoa_finite_size_2026"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/evidence/ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024","id":"field:d13afee4d073450caa89dad52f416dbb6d412b3a57400468d89a5145ce9ba8af","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/evidence/ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"subject_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","id":"fi